    "title": "Redirect engine concepts",
    "description": "Redirect engine concepts — index to variables, conditionals, regex behavior, and edge-case limits.",
    "markdown": "# Redirect engine concepts\n\nThis section documents the LinkShift redirect engine in depth: placeholders, modifiers, conditional logic, and edge cases.\n\nFor rule configuration, matching modes, and link map integration, start with the [Redirect rules guide](../guides/redirect-rules.md).\n\n---\n\n## Engine concept guides\n\n| Guide | Topics |\n|-------|--------|\n| [Variables and modifiers](./redirect-engine-variables.md) | Request variables, modifiers, `{time()}`, `{random()}`, escaping, missing placeholders |\n| [Conditional routing](./redirect-engine-conditionals.md) | Ternary syntax, operators, live pipeline, routing decision diagram, queryMatch choice |\n| [Regex, link maps, and edge cases](./redirect-engine-edge-cases.md) | Regex and wildcard sources, link map key extraction, runtime edge cases, validation summary, quick reference, advanced FAQ |\n\n**Questions?** [FAQ and troubleshooting](../guides/faq.md) indexes overview FAQ, recipes, and [advanced engineering FAQ](./redirect-engine-edge-cases.md#advanced-engineering-faq).\n\nRelated: [Redirect rules guide](../guides/redirect-rules.md) · [Link map concepts](./link-map-concepts.md)"
